.TH SDL_HINT_WINDOWS_CLOSE_ON_ALT_F4 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_WINDOWS_CLOSE_ON_ALT_F4 \- A variable controlling whether SDL generates window-close events for Alt+F4 on Windows.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_WINDOWS_CLOSE_ON_ALT_F4 \(dqSDL_WINDOWS_CLOSE_ON_ALT_F4\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: SDL will only do normal key handling for Alt+F4\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: SDL will generate a window-close event when it sees Alt+F4\[char46] (default)
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

